{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1114712-how-many-players-developers-of-scion-actually-honor-the-old-gods","id":1114712,"title":"How Many Players/Developers of Scion Actually Honor the Old Gods?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-07-11T12:48:33-07:00","id":1114712,"title":"How Many Players/Developers of Scion Actually Honor the Old Gods?","content":"Hi,<br /> I am a individual with a strong connection to Mongan ap Fiachna, divine child of Manannan mac Lir. I am curious about how many people who love scion actually worship/venerate the old gods, or have a personal connection with them? I have seen so many passionate individuals supporting this &quot;game&quot; (I view it as a path of mysticism) that I can't help but think some others here have a similiar relationship.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13647-manannansun","name":"Manannansun","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"78"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-11T13:18:32-07:00","id":1114719,"title":"","content":"I remember that Neall mentioned that while he might not personally WORSHIP the Tuatha, he has a lot of Irish heritage, so he felt a sort of connection to learning about them for the project. I also remember seeing the introduction for the author of the Manitou mentioned that he's of Lakota heritage and lives out in Chicago.<br /> <br /> I mean, I wouldn't say that everyone has a deep personal connection, but I wouldn't be surprised if Neall tried to find writers who were passionate about their assigned pantheon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-11T14:17:26-07:00","id":1114747,"title":"","content":"There are members of the community who actively follow various entities or religious systems that are the topic of the game. Samudra, for example, is Hindu. As Kyman mentioned, there are a lot of developers or posters who seem to have a non-religious connection with various Pantheons as well. For example, my academic fascination for the Tuatha was fueled by one of my parents being Irish, and being able to use the Tuatha as a point of connecting with grandparents.<br /> <br /> I get the feeling there is a lot of that on the forum. People who do not necessarily worship the Pantheons depicted in the game, but have some sort of historical connection.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-11T22:32:28-07:00","id":1114929,"title":"","content":"I'm no pagan, but I've had at least one powerful spiritual exprience revolving around Het-Heru.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-12T13:06:56-07:00","id":1115214,"title":"","content":"I am pagan, although somewhat eclectic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-12T19:09:33-07:00","id":1115336,"title":"","content":"I identify very seriously as &quot;the religion of the person I'm speaking with at the time.&quot; That said, when I go looking for organized religion, it's Afro-Atlantic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-family:courier new\"><a href=\"https://jamesmendezhodes.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Mendez</span></a></span></div> <span style=\"font-family:courier new\"><b>Currently Developing</b> you know I should probably stop updating this field, I keep accidentally announcing things early<br /> <b>Crowdfund Me </b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mndz\" target=\"_blank\">via Patreon</a>: essays about race, religion, and culture in gaming</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8310-lula","name":"Lula","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8310_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-12T19:35:07-07:00","id":1115341,"title":"","content":"Honor yes, worship no.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-12T20:03:55-07:00","id":1115342,"title":"","content":"I used to be a huge fan of Greek mythology when I was younger and considered it an interesting religion.<br /> <br /> Then I got older, put the mythology into better context and realized what a bunch of dicks the Olympians were! (seriously, only the best and the brightest get into paradise when they die. The rest are thrown in the trash.)<br /> <br /> That being said, I am still fascinated by pagan mysticism and would still be interested in learning more about it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 07-12-2017, 11:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-12T21:17:51-07:00","id":1115375,"title":"","content":"As Watcher mentioned above, I'm Hindu, though my personal approach is a little eclectic, and best described as left-handed Pantheistic Shaktism with a Bhakti bent, with Kali as my personal patron, though I honour most of the Goddesses and Gods of all Pantheons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1344-samudra","name":"Samudra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1344_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"497"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-13T10:49:30-07:00","id":1115589,"title":"","content":"I was a little more active during the kickstarter and have mostly become a lurker these days, but I am pagan. I honor the Norse and Irish pantheons, with my personal deities being Thor, Brigid, Freyja, and Lugh. For me, being pagan is in part about reclaiming my ancestry. I have Viking ancestors on my dad's side and very strong Irish heritage on my mom's side. <br /> <br /> Part of the reason I love Scion so much is because I had never heard of the Tuatha before I read about them in the 1E Companion, so Scion helped me learn about a part of my heritage I probably wouldn't have learned about otherwise.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9296-zeldafan42","name":"Zeldafan42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9296_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"43"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-13T23:52:23-07:00","id":1115826,"title":"","content":"I honour the Norse gods, with a personal bent toward Thor, Freyja, and Loki (I know. Eclectic, right?). Tyr and Odin have also wandered in and out of my life before, Tyr especially, but day to day it's usually the first three.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2608-squee","name":"Squee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2608_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"120"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-15T00:27:44-07:00","id":1116283,"title":"","content":"I follow a personal path that generally deviates between the local variants of Shinto, Dao, Buddhist, and Kong Zi thought. Various aspects appeal to me, and I am still looking for further understanding as I go. I don't have a good way to explain it, but I wouldn't call it either Honor or Worship, its something other than that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>How can I know if what I claim I know to be true is rejecting the idea that there is something I might not know? How can I know if what I claim I don't know to be true is rejecting the idea that there is something I do know?<br /> -Zhuangzi","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1715-ostarion","name":"Ostarion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1715_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"305"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-15T01:30:14-07:00","id":1116295,"title":"","content":"I just realized I didn't put my personal read down, and if we're taking this to a &quot;What Do The Gods Of Old Mean To You?&quot; I'll happily post my thoughts.<br /> <br /> I personally don't consider myself especially religious. But I <i>am</i> fascinated by <i>stories</i>. I love learning about different religions, academically.<br /> <br /> I also don't begrudge people of their faith if they're not using it as an excuse to be a jackass. Personally I feel that these myths and religions exist to help bring people peace and help make sense of this crazy world of ours. If your faith helps bring you peace or inspires you to be a better person, then bless you. The world could use more like you.<br /> <br /> Though alas, I'm one of those &quot;Freaking Casuals&quot; when it comes to myths. More familiar with the Greek, Nordic, and Egyptian myths than the others... Though many of my grade school classes had units on the myths and stories of the Native tribes of the Pacific Northwest (the Washington State area to be specific). But that's why I love both the variety of the Pantheons we're getting in 2E, and the <i>very</i> obvious passion that the writers are putting in. I'd love to learn more, and I think this new Scion edition will be <i>great</i> for that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-16T19:43:10-07:00","id":1117054,"title":"","content":"I am personally an atheist. I believe mythology to be fiction, but nevertheless, it's fascinating fiction. I can appreciate the old gods as interesting characters, cultural icons, and a fascinating view into the nature of humanity. Mythology is a great display of how humankind changes, yet nevertheless, retains certain universal, narrative constants, even between the most varied of cultures. On top of that, it's just cool. From the epic, apocalyptic, battle of Ragnarok to Kali massacring hordes of Raktavija clones by slurping up their blood, mythology has all the tropes and elements I love in all sorts of fiction. It's also a great source of inspiration for me creatively. I love coming up with new stories about these figures. I'm particularly fascinated by crossover cosmologies, as I love seeing interactions between beings of widely varied natures and cultural origins, and I'm quite intrigued by the question of what the old gods are doing in modern times. I also, needless to say, love researching the more obscure of the world's mythical figures. I love using figures from little-known mythologies from underrepresented cultures, both because I feel those people's figures and stories need to be represented and there's also an enormous amount of untapped potential for fiction from those little-known stories.<br /> <br /> I confess I can sometimes get a bit smug and bitter when it comes to religion, fuelled to a great degree by the far-less-then-positive effect the Christian right, in particular, has had in the US where I live, but overall, concerning people of faith, if you're not a bigot, and you don't deny science, and you're pro separation of church and state, I don't have a problem with you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13079-wannabe-demon-lord","name":"Wannabe Demon Lord","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"286"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-18T08:18:35-07:00","id":1117746,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1114712-how-many-players-developers-of-scion-actually-honor-the-old-gods?p=1115341#post1115341\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honor yes, worship no.</div> </div> </div> </div>I identify as some sort of eclectic. I agree with Glamour, given that I honor the gods and such, but im not entirely sure how to worship some of them and other than tithing a small bit of food and some energy, i dont do much.<br /> <br /> I'm not religious, I just believe. I believe in the gods as they are, and continue to learn about them as i can. <br /> I ask them for help and give praise to the gods, they have my faith and belief, but i'll honor them in my own ways, not via a religious way. <br /> <br /> The Theoi and Tuatha are pantheons i follow a bit more closely than the others, and i work to learn and understand more of the other pantheons. mythology fascinates me, so i enjoy learning more of the stories.<br /> <br /> people can believe what they wish. its not my decision as to what you believe.<br /> <br /> have a lovely day!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8023-grimangel53","name":"Grimangel53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"68"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-18T08:27:55-07:00","id":1117755,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1114712-how-many-players-developers-of-scion-actually-honor-the-old-gods?p=1114719#post1114719\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, I wouldn't say that everyone has a deep personal connection, but I wouldn't be surprised if Neall tried to find writers who were passionate about their assigned pantheon.</div> </div> </div> </div>He certainly did! Finding the right authors was one of the most important parts of the project.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-18T11:14:54-07:00","id":1117860,"title":"","content":"\u00c1satr\u00faar here, have been so for over 30 years.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Lead Writer for the Savage Age of Werewolf: the Apocalypse: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/428750/Ghost-Lineages-The-Advanced-Players-Guide-to-the-Savage-Age\" target=\"_blank\">Ghost Lineages</a>, <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/312700/The-Rise-of-the-Garou-The-Savage-Age-Volume-Two\" target=\"_blank\">Rise of the Garou</a>, <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/331302/Tools-of-Extinction-The-Savage-Age-Volume-Three\" target=\"_blank\">Tools of Extinction</a>, <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/352717/Tribebook-Wlewa\" target=\"_blank\">Tribebook: Wlewa</a>.<br /> <br /> Want RPGs in libraries? Check out my book, <a href=\"http://www.abc-clio.com/ABC-CLIOCorporate/product.aspx?pc=A3951P\" target=\"_blank\">Dragons in the Stacks</a>. Now with <a href=\"http://www.ennie-awards.com/blog/2015-ennie-award-nominees-and-spotlight-winners/\" target=\"_blank\">awards</a>!<br /> \u200b","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1813-grimjaws","name":"grimjaws","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1813_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"134"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-18T21:35:08-07:00","id":1118066,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>grimjaws</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1114712-how-many-players-developers-of-scion-actually-honor-the-old-gods?p=1117860#post1117860\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u00c1satr\u00faar here, have been so for over 30 years.</div> </div> </div> </div>Could you explain what that means?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>How can I know if what I claim I know to be true is rejecting the idea that there is something I might not know? How can I know if what I claim I don't know to be true is rejecting the idea that there is something I do know?<br /> -Zhuangzi","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1715-ostarion","name":"Ostarion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1715_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"305"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-19T01:08:48-07:00","id":1118105,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ostarion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1114712-how-many-players-developers-of-scion-actually-honor-the-old-gods?p=1118066#post1118066\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Could you explain what that means?</div> </div> </div> </div>Modern adherent to the Norse gods.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-19T03:33:58-07:00","id":1118122,"title":"","content":"Originally from Macau, I learned to pray different Shens which looked more superstition than anything now that I think about it. I would burn papers for the Gods and the ancestors, I would light incense to the different gods and respect particuarly Guanyin, looking for mercy and health whenever my family needed it. My aunt taunt me and it was like a game. I was the only one receptive to that because mythology has always fascinated me. <br /> <br /> I tried and still want to apply the Wiccan way but I feel like not ready to be that gentle and nice to everyone hehe. I feel like religion would force me to accomplish things that I would not have done if I werent a believer. <br /> <br /> The bigger picture sounds good but the path that brings to that picture never seemed right enough.<br /> <br /> It is still fun to know that all that existed and still exist. What is fun about mythology is that it looks fictional. I exclude monotheism because it is not glamourous... and well, brought too many conflicts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1837-wickedgrail","name":"Wickedgrail","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1837_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-19T17:16:11-07:00","id":1118317,"title":"","content":"I identify as Wiccan, but I've strayed from the way the majority of Wiccans view the divine, so realistically, I guess the best way to describe myself would be as an eclectic polytheist. I mostly focus on the Greco-Roman, Celtic and Germanic gods, but I am open to the idea that every god and goddess of every pantheon is equally real, and even if I don't worship them personally, I respect them. Oh, and for the record, Wicca doesn't require you to be gentle and nice to everyone, you just aren't allowed to &quot;harm&quot; anyone. And different Wiccans view that concept differently, with some making exceptions for self-defense, or only counting physical harm and not mental or emotional harm, etc. That's the thing about practicing a revealed religion vs an organized religion, different covens view things very differently, and every solitary practitioner has their own way of doing things <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13472-~nkf~","name":"~NKF~","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"25"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-19T20:40:06-07:00","id":1118394,"title":"","content":"idk about the writers, but i love Scion and i have been a witch for the last 15 years. i am a member of the Kemetic Orthodox Church and daughter of Bast.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2197-roleplayrose","name":"roleplayrose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2197_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-20T10:13:40-07:00","id":1118600,"title":"","content":"Also, confession time. I got what the OP meant in the initial title, but for an instant I saw &quot;Honor the Old Gods&quot; and my brain went to &quot;Ia Ia Cthulu Fhtagn!&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-28T01:09:29-07:00","id":1121750,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1114712-how-many-players-developers-of-scion-actually-honor-the-old-gods?p=1118600#post1118600\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, confession time. I got what the OP meant in the initial title, but for an instant I saw &quot;Honor the Old Gods&quot; and my brain went to &quot;Ia Ia Cthulu Fhtagn!&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>If I had read that, Game of Thrones would have come up in my mind first!<br /> <br /> @NKF not to harm means to be nice and kind to me and of course I include mental harm, which is the worst for me. I won't feel whole if I act in a way to... circumvent the rules. I'd rather not be Wiccan yet <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1837,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1837-wickedgrail","user":"Wickedgrail","date":". 07-28-2017, 04:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1837-wickedgrail","name":"Wickedgrail","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1837_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"199"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}